    "model_design": "Change #1: [Model Architecture: GCN with multiple tasks] Replace the MLP with a Graph Isomorphism Network (GIN) followed by global mean pooling and task-specific MLP heads. The GIN will have 4 layers, hidden dimension 256, and use batch normalization and dropout. The task-specific heads will be 2-layer MLPs (256->64->1). This architecture is known to be effective for molecular property prediction (e.g., from the Open Graph Benchmark). The model will output normalized predictions for all 9 targets. Update the loss function to use the same masked SmoothL1 loss but with the new model's output shape."
